cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this Lean formalization, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "one-phase-critical-dim: flatness of one-homogeneous one-phase Bernoulli minimizers in dimensions at most six, in Lean"
version: "0.1.1"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/willmfeldman/one-phase-critical-dim"
authors:
  - family-names: Feldman
    given-names: "William M."
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 / Mathlib proof that, for 1 ≤ d ≤ 6, every nonnegative, nonzero, one-homogeneous global
  minimizer of the one-phase Bernoulli energy in ℝᵈ is flat. The proof follows the
  universal-certificate method of the preprint "The critical dimension for one-phase Bernoulli
  minimizers"; the classical regularity theory it uses, and the classification in dimensions at
  most four, are proved rather than assumed.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formalized mathematics
  - free boundary problems
  - Bernoulli problem
  - one-phase problem
  - minimal cones
